      "RWR",
      "[Expert R1] (Detect atomicity violations in the code.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[System] Expert first round completed in 3.19 seconds\n\n[Judge R1] (Validate the expert's defect report and check control/interrupt conditions.)\nLet me analyze each read/write operation for the global variable `j` to determine if the reported atomicity violation is valid.\n\n## Analysis of Read/Write Operations for Variable `j`\n\n### 1. Read operation at line 14: `i = j + 1;`\n- **Location**: `svp_simple_329_001_isr_1`, inside a for loop\n- **Control condition**: `k < NUM` where `k` is initialized to 0 and incremented by 1 each iteration\n- **Variable value tracking**: \n  - `k` starts at 0 and increments to NUM-1 (9)\n  - The loop condition `k < NUM` is satisfied for k = 0,1,2,...,9\n- **Execution**: This read operation will execute 10 times when `svp_simple_329_001_isr_1` runs\n\n### 2. Write operation at line 20: `j = i + 1;`\n- **Location**: `svp_simple_329_001_isr_2`, inside a for loop\n- **Control condition**: `k < NUM` where `k` is initialized to 0 and incremented by 1 each iteration\n- **Variable value tracking**:\n  - `k` starts at 0 and increments to NUM-1 (9)\n  - The loop condition `k < NUM` is satisfied for k = 0,1,2,...,9\n- **Execution**: This write operation will execute 10 times when `svp_simple_329_001_isr_2` runs\n\n### 3. Read operation at line 14 (second occurrence): `i = j + 1;`\n- This is the same read operation as the first one, just referenced again in the pattern\n\n## Interrupt Status Analysis\n- The code does not contain any `disable_isr()` or `enable_isr()` calls\n- Both ISRs (interrupt service routines) can preempt each other based on their priorities\n- `svp_simple_329_001_isr_1` has priority 1 (higher priority)\n- `svp_simple_329_001_isr_2` has priority 2 (lower priority)\n\n## Summary of Analysis\n- **All operations can be executed**: \n  - The read at line 14 can execute when `svp_simple_329_001_isr_1` runs\n  - The write at line 20 can execute when `svp_simple_329_001_isr_2` runs\n  - There are no control conditions that prevent these operations from executing\n  - There are no interrupt disable mechanisms preventing ISR execution\n\n- **Atomicity violation exists**: The pattern shows a read of `j` in ISR1, followed by a write to `j` in ISR2, followed by another read of `j` in ISR1. This creates a potential atomicity violation since ISR1 (priority 1) can preempt ISR2 (priority 2), leading to non-atomic access to the shared variable `j`.\n\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n[Expert R2] (Refine the report based on judge feedback, re-check for missed or false defects.)\n```json\n{\n    \"violations\": [\n        {\n            \"sharedVariable\": \"j\",\n            \"accessPattern\": [\"Read\", \"Write\", \"Read\"],\n            \"lines\": [14, 20, 14]\n        }\n    ]\n}\n```\n\n"
